      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y'&=2e^x\\\\y'(1)&=2e\\end{align*}$$\nThe tangent has gradient $m_T=2e$. At $x=1$, $y=2e$, so the point is $(1,2e)$.\nUsing the point-gradient formula,\n$$\\begin{align*}y-2e&=2e(x-1)\\\\y&=2ex\\end{align*}$$",
